From: Paul Zhang <paul@studio-vaai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mf2-locale-data, mf2-build: cut the ICU4X date backend

`icu-blob` writes ICU4X's date data into catalogs, through
`mf2-fn-datetime` and a dozen ICU4X crates. The SDK formats no dates in
messages and does not vendor `mf2-fn-datetime`, so the optional dependency
would resolve to the crates.io copies of `mf2-fn-datetime`, `mf2-runtime`,
`mf2-catalog` and `mf2-model` beside the vendored ones (the lockfile lists
a workspace member's optional dependencies whether or not they build).

Both manifests lose the feature, its dependencies and the `icu_blob` test
target; the upstream pin's drop list removes `tests/icu_blob.rs`. The code
behind `feature = "icu-blob"`, `src/icu_blob.rs` among it, stays as it is,
never compiled in, with the name declared to `check-cfg` so it draws no
warning: a smaller patch than deleting it from `mf2-build`.

Upstream: local only
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
diff --git a/mf2-build/Cargo.toml b/mf2-build/Cargo.toml
index 320a2aa..bc4f635 100644
--- a/mf2-build/Cargo.toml
+++ b/mf2-build/Cargo.toml
@@ -52,12 +52,8 @@ license = "MIT"
 repository = "https://github.com/EvanCarroll/rust-mf2"
 
 [package.metadata.docs.rs]
-features = ["icu-blob"]
 targets = ["x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu"]
 
-[features]
-icu-blob = ["mf2-locale-data/icu-blob"]
-
 [lib]
 name = "mf2_build"
 path = "src/lib.rs"
@@ -159,3 +155,6 @@ priority = -1
 missing_debug_implementations = "allow"
 unreachable_pub = "warn"
 unsafe_code = "deny"
+# The ICU4X date backend is cut: code behind `feature = "icu-blob"` never
+# compiles in, and the name is known so it draws no warning.
+unexpected_cfgs = { level = "warn", check-cfg = ['cfg(feature, values("icu-blob"))'] }
